@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+# Finite code-point preprocessing
+
+`CodePointInput.preprocess` accepts a finite `List (Fin 0x110000)`, including
+surrogate code points, and returns `List Char`. The old `CssInput` scalar API is
+unchanged. `scalar_refinement` proves identical results when its scalar inputs
+are embedded in the larger domain.
+
+`CssCodePointInput` defines the executable algorithm and an independent inductive
+`Point`/`Preprocess` relation. `CssCodePointInputLaws` proves exact correspondence,
+uniqueness, normalized output, nonexpansion and the surrogate replacement rule.
+`CssCodePointInputRefinement` proves scalar compatibility and idempotence under
+scalar re-embedding. `CssCodePointInputExamples` supplies 21 ordered, kernel-checked
+observations, also registered in the standard executable runner. All 27 named
+theorems are registered in the standard axiom audit.
+
+## Source and interpretation
+
+The mapping from English prose to both Lean definitions is manually authored and
+reviewed. Kernel checking proves the model's internal correspondence and laws;
+it does not prove that the prose was interpreted correctly or that Firefox
+implements this model.
+
+The source is CSS Syntax 3 [input preprocessing](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-syntax-3/#input-preprocessing),
+pinned to [Overview.bs at c410ee5e4d2afe6d8b2e8ce53723b8d1eb3b5b67](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/blob/c410ee5e4d2afe6d8b2e8ce53723b8d1eb3b5b67/css-syntax-3/Overview.bs).
+Its SHA-256 is `4a4a5a3994bda10a56885e66776169d0e05d5a7515b0def4e8859c20e3fd4afc`.
+CRLF becomes one LF; CR and FF become LF; NUL and surrogates become U+FFFD.
+The separate CRLF relation constructor and single-point exclusion preserve that
+pair boundary. Ordinary relation outputs are `Char`, whose scalar validity
+excludes surrogate preservation.
+
+The code-point domain and surrogate ranges come from
+[Infra at c67ae1fb1d161b23d0f8c9bf9917ea1993f7b19a](https://github.com/whatwg/infra/blob/c67ae1fb1d161b23d0f8c9bf9917ea1993f7b19a/infra.bs),
+SHA-256 `687e65669b9d85c2147a139513fe319097cf84af1005f5c9d7cb3d2ade0c1aed`.
+Both source paths were acquired on 2026-11-10 and are recorded independently
+in `coverage.json`. Source hashes establish provenance, not semantic correctness.
+
+## Admission and boundaries
+
+Use `ofNat?` or `filterValues` to admit external natural numbers. They reject
+values above U+10FFFF. A numeric `Fin` literal can wrap; it is not a validation
+interface. Admission failure is outside the model's code-point domain, not a
+CSS parse error. Noncharacters, supplied U+FEFF and U+2028/U+2029 are preserved.
+
+This input is already a list of code points. Byte decoding, encoding detection,
+BOM decoding policy and WebIDL/DOMString/UTF-16 conversion are separate concerns
+and are not modeled. Supplied `[0xd83d, 0xde00]` means two surrogate code points,
+so both are replaced. It does not describe conversion of a valid UTF-16 pair.
+
+The domain is finite lists. There is no live-stream or chunked-processing proof:
+filtering `[CR, LF]` together yields one LF, while filtering each singleton and
+concatenating yields two. A streaming adapter needs pending-CR state and its own
+correspondence theorem. Existing scalar tokenizer entry points are unchanged;
+the new layer does not claim a new whole-source or browser integration.
+
+## Checks
+
+`python3 check.py` retains the full build, executable examples and axiom audit.
+`python3 check.py --coverage-only` performs the same static declaration/audit and
+coverage-link checks without a Lean build. This mode is a registration check, not
+proof verification, and does not replace a full verification receipt.
+
+This addition was checked from clean source for its dependency closure, including
+the unchanged scalar module and its 24 prior examples. No whole-library or
+browser result is refreshed by that scoped check. The earlier isolated model
+also rejected eight executable semantic mutations; those historical controls
+are separate from the canonical integration receipt.
